<kml xmlns="http://www.opengis.net/kml/2.2"><Document><name>Recorded surfer and drone GPS</name><description>Logged points within the requested window. Green: accepted surfer packets; orange: other/rejected surfer packets; blue: drone-position snapshots. Red overrides either subject colour when retreat was active at any point in that reporting interval. Repeated snapshots are retained, not new independent GPS fixes. Click a point for timestamp, GPS age if logged, source and original record. Times are observation/receipt times. Ground-clamped display, not flight altitude. Short arrows show bearing from the previous logged coordinate of the same subject, not aircraft heading or an observed path. Arrow length is display-only. No arrow for unchanged positions or the first point. A gap label identifies intervals over 1.5s. No connecting tracks or saved targets used as GPS observations.</description><Style id="surfer"><IconStyle><color>ff00cc00</color><scale>0.65</scale><Icon><href>https://maps.google.com/mapfiles/kml/shapes/placemark_circle.png</href></Icon></IconStyle><LabelStyle><scale>0.85</scale></LabelStyle><LineStyle><color>ff00cc00</color><width>2</width></LineStyle></Style><Style id="surfer_arrow"><LabelStyle><scale>0</scale></LabelStyle><LineStyle><color>ff00cc00</color><width>2</width></LineStyle></Style><Folder><name>Surfer — accepted packets</name><Placemark><name>R1-S1</name><styleUrl>#surfer</styleUrl><description>Logged time: 2026-10-30T14:03:21.724+10:00
